**********Angular Interpolation************
What is Interpolation
-> Display data from TS to HTML file.
-> whenever we make any component in angular logic is in app.ts and data is written in app.html.
{{name}}
->interpolation
when anything is inside {{}} it will check whether it is present in app.ts or not as a property if it is not then it will shtart doing its calculation as js but even if that is also not it will give error

<h1>{{10+23+45}} </h1> -> correct
<h1>{{name = 20;}} </h1> -> wrong
<h1>{{getName()}}</h1>

app.ts  getName(a: number , b: number){ // whenever we use any parameter in typescript we have to //declare ther type
    return this.name;
}
if we are making any function inside an class and we want to use any var made in class then we have to use this.var_name;

->One wy data binding - from component to template.
app.ts-> app.html => correct  app.html -> app.ts => cant send therefore one way data binding.
->Angular automatically updates the view  whenever the value in the components changes.{{34+224+24}}
->You can use expressions, but avoid complex logic or side-effects inside interpolation
->Safe from Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)(it can misuse data , can damage security issue) as Angular automatically sanitizes the output
->No complex calculations or heavy functions-- do those in the component

we can use html in app.ts in template:`<h1> Inline template {{name}}</h1>`
we can use  interpolation in Inline template also.



