***********Signals*********
Signal is a wrapper around a value.It give a signal when value changes.
count = signal(10);
count = 10;
it will show in both ui ans ts file that a var is changed unlike without signal which show only on ui.


********Type of Signals**********
A writable signal is a signal whose value we can change
A computed signal is a read-only signal , Derived Signals
Effect signal: Runs side effect when signals change

Signals Vs Normal properties

Reactivity              Reactive(Angular tracks changes)        Not Reactive
UI Update               Auto update UI when value change        Depends on change detection
Change detection        Fine-grained only affected parts        Full component check
Syntax                  count()                                 count
Update                  set()/update()                          Direct assignment
Performance             Faster,optimized                        Slower for large Apps

signals are faster that state in react.

************Computed Signals***********

computed signals cant be directly updated.
if any update happen signal give update regarding it.nd then effect can happen on that basis.


*************Effects in Angular*************
used in constructor . If any signal is inside that effect then if signal update effect will also call.
avoid  updating signal in effect.

